==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|tarif}}, from {{der|en|it|tariffa}}, from {{der|en|ota|تعرفه|tr=ta'rife}}, from {{der|en|fa|تعرفه|tr=ta'refe}}, from {{der|en|ar|تَعْرِفَة||tariff, rate}}, from the root {{ar-root|ع|ر|ف|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtæɹɪf/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[system]] of [[government]]-[[impose]]d [[duties]] [[levied]] on [[import]]ed or [[export]]ed [[goods]]; a [[list]] of such duties, or the duties themselves.
#:* ''The European Union and Japan signed a huge free trade deal on Tuesday that cuts or eliminates '''tariffs''' on nearly all goods.'' —  CNN — EU and Japan sign trade deal covering a third of the world's economy — 17 july 2018
# A [[schedule]] of [[rate]]s, [[fee]]s or [[price]]s.
# {{lb|en|British}} A [[sentence]] determined according to a [[scale]] of [[standard]] [[penalties]] for certain [[categories]] of [[crime]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|tariffless}}

